            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0800" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/327: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-17T11:00:00+08:00">April 17, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 17—4:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to last paragraph of your telegram 121, March 29, 5 p.m., I learn
                    that the Chinese Government for various reasons does not consider it expedient
                    to take the matter up through its Legation in Washington and that Soong is
                    therefore continuing his conversations with Trade Commissioner Howard here
                    regarding civilian aviation. Has the Department any objection?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
